{title: My Strength}
{subtitle: Psalms 59:17}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Consume them in [Bb]wrath
Till they are no [Gm]more
Then they will know
[Eb]God rules over Ja[Fsus4]cob
To the ends of the [Bb]earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They return at evening
Snarling like [Gm]dogs
Prowling around the c[Eb]ity
Roaming for [Fsus4]food
If not filled they [Eb]howl
Through the [Fsus4]dark night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But I will [Eb]sing of your [Bb]strength
In the morn[Gm]ing I will sing a[F]loud
Of your mer[Eb]cy
For you have been [Gm]my fortress
My [Fsus4]refuge in my dis[Eb]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
O my [Bb]Strength
To you I sing [Gm]praise
For God is my [Eb]fortress
My God of [Fsus4]mer[F]cy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I will [Eb]sing of your [Bb]strength
In the morn[Gm]ing I will sing a[F]loud
Of your mer[Eb]cy
For you have been [Gm]my fortress
My [Fsus4]refuge in my dis[Eb]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [F] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In the [Eb]day of my dis[Bb]tress
You are [Gm]my fortress
My God of [F]mercy
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I will [Eb]sing of your [Bb]strength
In the morn[Gm]ing I will sing a[F]loud
Of your mer[Eb]cy
For you have been [Gm]my fortress
My [F]refuge in my dis[Eb]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
O my [Bb]Strength
To you I sing [Gm][Eb]praise
{end_of_verse}
